# Git Conventions

- Never commit directly to `main`.
- Use descriptive branch names prefixed with developer names or features (e.g. `pranav/repo-env-init`).
- Write commits using Conventional Commit labels: `feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, `chore:`.
- Ensure all CI tests pass before submitting and merging pull requests.
